// PARAM: --analysis congruence --context entry-state
// The context-sensitive counterpart 05-congruence_across_call.vimp names.
// triple has two call sites carrying different singleton classes. Joined at
// one context, p is the congruence join of 4 and 5 -- gcd(|4-5|) = 1, so
// 1 (mod 1), every integer -- and return_congruence publishes p * 3 as
// 0 (mod 3), which decides neither check: --analysis congruence alone
// answers UNKNOWN twice with a==0 (mod 3), b==0 (mod 3).
//
// Under entry-state contexts the two call sites seed triple separately,
// each with its own singleton, so combine reads back 12 and 15 exactly.
// The entry-state route is the whole content of this case: the same
// program, the same domain, decided only because the contexts stay apart.
fun triple(p) { return p * 3; }
fun main() {
  a = triple(4);
  b = triple(5);
  __voblint_check(a == 12); // PROVED
  __voblint_check(b == 15); // PROVED
}
